\fs48 \cf2 Add the VS Code extension\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 If you're using {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://code.visualstudio.com/"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Visual Studio Code}} or another IDE derived from it (such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cursor.com/home"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Cursor}}), we recommend installing the Mojo extension, which provides features like syntax highlighting, code completion, and debugging support. You can install it from either:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=modular-mojotools.vscode-mojo"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Visual Studio Code Marketplace}}, for VS Code users\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://open-vsx.org/extension/modular-mojotools/vscode-mojo"}}{\fldrslt \cf5 \ul \ulc5 Open VSX Registry}}, for users of Cursor and other editors that support VS Code extensions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Or, open the Extensions view in your IDE and search for "Mojo"\'97make sure you install the extension from Modular.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa127\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb13 Prior to the 0.25.6 Mojo release, there were two versions of the Mojo extension: a stable version for working with the stable build of Mojo and a nightly version for working with the nightly build of Mojo. Concurrent with the 0.25.6 Mojo release, we've consolidated the two versions into a single extension that works for both stable and nightly builds.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb13 The new extension replaces the old stable version, so if you have the stable version installed, you can simply update it to receive the new version. If you have the nightly version of the extension installed, you should uninstall it and install the regular (non-nightly) version.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

